lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-csf
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_CSF" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_CSF
    skos:definition "G.8021 - ETH layer: Reception of a CSF frame that indicates a client loss of signal (dCSF-LOS) or a client forward defect indication (dCSF-FDI) or a client reverse defect indication (dCSF-RDI).\nThe CSF (CSF-LOS, CSF-FDI, and CSF-RDI) defect is calculated at the ETH layer. It monitors the presence of a CSF maintenance signal.\nG.8021 - GFP: dCSF is Client-specific GFP-F and GFP-T (resp. Frame and Transparent) sink processes.\ndCSF-RDI: GFP client signal fail-remote defect indication is raised when a GFP client management frame with the RDI UPI (as defined in Table 6-4 of [ITU-T G.7041]) is received.\ndCSF-RDI is cleared when no such GFP client management frame is received in N x 1000 ms (a value of 3 is suggested for N), a valid GFP client data frame is received, or a GFP client management frame with the DCI UPI is received.\ndCSF-FDI: GFP client signal fail-forward defect indication is raised when a GFP client management frame with the FDI UPI (as defined in Table 6-4 of [ITU-T G.7041]) is received.\ndCSF-FDI is cleared when no such GFP client management frame is received in N x 1000 ms (a value of 3 is suggested for N), a valid GFP client data frame is received, or a GFP client management frame with the DCI UPI is received.\ndCSF-LOS: GFP client signal fail-loss of signal is raised when a GFP client management frame with the LOS UPI (as defined in Table 6-4 of [ITU-T G.7041]) is received.\ndCSF-LOS is cleared when no such GFP client management frame is received in N x 1000 ms (a value of 3 is suggested for N), a valid GFP client data frame is received, or a GFP client management frame with the DCI UPI is received." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_CSF> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-degraded
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_DEGRADED" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_DEGRADED
    skos:definition "G.8021: The defect is detected if there are MI_LM_DEGM (lmDegm of EthMepSink) consecutive bad seconds and cleared if there are MI_LM_M (lmM of EthMepSink) consecutive good seconds.\nIn order to declare a bad second the number of transmitted frames must exceed a threshold (MI_LM_TFMIN, lmTfMin of EthMepSink).\nFurthermore, if the frame loss ratio (lost frames/transmitted frames) is greater than MI_LM_DEGTHR (lmDegThr of EthMepSink), a bad second is declared.\nThis defect is only defined for point-to-point ETH connections. It monitors the connectivity of an ETH trail.\n" ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_DEGRADED> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-exm
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_EXM" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_EXM
    skos:definition "G.806 - Common GFP sink processes: GFP extension header mismatch (dEXM) is raised when the accepted EXI (AcEXI) is different from the expected EXI.\ndEXM is cleared when AcEXI matches the expected EXI or GFP_SF is active." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_EXM> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-lfd
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LFD" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LFD
    skos:definition "G.806 - Server layer-specific GFP sink processes: GFP loss of frame delineation (dLFD) is raised when the frame delineation process (clause 6.3.1 of [ITU-T G.7041]) is not in the 'SYNC' state.\ndLFD is cleared when the frame delineation process is in the 'SYNC' state." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LFD> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-locked
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LOCKED" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LOCKED
    skos:definition "G.8021: Reception of a LCK frame." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LOCKED> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-loss-of-continuity
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LOSS_OF_CONTINUITY" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LOSS_OF_CONTINUITY
    skos:definition "G.8021: The loss of continuity defect is calculated at the ETH layer. It monitors the presence of continuity in ETH trails." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_LOSS_OF_CONTINUITY> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-mismerge-unexpected-meg
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_MISMERGE_UNEXPECTED_MEG" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_MISMERGE_UNEXPECTED_MEG
    skos:definition "G.8021: Reception of a CCM frame with an invalid MEG value, but with a valid MEL value.\nMonitoring of the connectivity in a maintenance entity group.\n" ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_MISMERGE_UNEXPECTED_MEG> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-partial-link-loss
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_PARTIAL_LINK_LOSS" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_PARTIAL_LINK_LOSS
    skos:definition "G.8021: LAG - fault cause shall be raised if the number of active ports is less than the provisioned threshold." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_PARTIAL_LINK_LOSS> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-plm
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_PLM" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_PLM
    skos:definition "G.806: The payload label mismatch defect (dPLM) shall be detected if the 'accepted TSL' code does not match the 'expected TSL' code. If the 'accepted TSL' is 'equipped non-specific', the mismatch is not detected (TSL: Trail Signal Label).\nPayload type supervision checks that compatible adaptation functions are used at the source and the sink.\nThis is normally done by adding a signal type identifier at the source adaptation function and comparing it with the expected identifier at the sink.\nIf they do not match, a payload mismatch is detected." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_PLM> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-rdi
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_RDI" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_RDI
    skos:definition "G.8021: Remote defect indicator defect, reception by an MEP (indexed by 'i', this index not included in the 'cause' cRDI) of a CCM frame with valid MEL, MEG, MEP and periodicity values and the RDI flag set to x; where x=0 (remote defect clear) and x=1 (remote defect set)." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_RDI> .

lex:tapi-eth-eth-alarm-condition-name-total-link-loss
    a lex:ReferenceEntry ;
    skos:prefLabel "ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_TOTAL_LINK_LOSS" ;
    # source: http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_TOTAL_LINK_LOSS
    skos:definition "G.8021: LAG - fault cause will be raised if no ports are active for an aggregator." ;
    lex:canonicalExample "" ;
    lex:entityClass lex:IdentityKind ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/ontology/identity/tapi-eth/ETH_ALARM_CONDITION_NAME_TOTAL_LINK_LOSS> .

